<decision #track.add_typed_navigation_property_model.member_authority { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low; collapsing Property into Field or Relation would break the restored authority boundary" } (
  <question ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRQ>
  typed navigation property 应复用 field、top-level relation，还是成为独立 class member kind？
  </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRQ>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRR>
    property 必须与 field 区分，并服务 Order.shop 等 class property。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRR>
    <decision-text ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRS>
    新增独立 Property member kind；top-level RelationTypeSymbol 保持 schema/ontology primitive。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRS>
    <rationale ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRT>
    field alias 会限制复合关系，relation primitive 又不等于对象可导航属性。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRT>
    <evidence ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRV>
    用户明确要求与当前 runtime class field/prop 区分一致。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRV>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.add_typed_navigation_property_model.kind_semantics { priority = "P0" status = "resolved" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low; ambiguous cross-kind resolution would make the discriminator non-authoritative" } (
  <question ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRW>
  Field、Property、Method、Spread 的 compatibility 与 runtime boundary 如何定义？
  </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRW>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRX>
    采用严格同 kind compatibility，并保留既有 Field-to-zero-arg-Method adaptation；无 accessor typed property 为 model-only。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRX>
    <decision-text ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRY>
    slot access 只解析 value members，receiver call 只解析 Method；同 origin 或 inheritance 的跨 kind 同名替换失败；typed inline accessor 无需影子 Method 即可执行，伴生 Method signature 必须服从 property type；缺失 accessor 的 runtime read/write 返回 property-specific error。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRY>
    <rationale ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRZ>
    Kind 必须参与 compatibility 和 resolution 才能成为真 discriminator，同时 model-only property 支持 DSL 建模且不伪装 field storage。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PRZ>
    <evidence ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS0>
    planning AttractorCheck GAP 对 subtype、lookup、accessor、runtime fallback 和 copy path 的代码证据。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS0>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.add_typed_navigation_property_model.type_admission { priority = "P0" status = "resolved" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "medium; future inference may supplement but not replace explicit schema types" } (
  <question ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS1>
  binder 是否应从 getter body 推断 property 类型？
  </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS1>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS2>
    采用显式 property type 作为保守默认。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS2>
    <decision-text ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS3>
    只有显式 typed prop 进入 property row member；accessor-only prop 不做 Any/field 推断。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS3>
    <rationale ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS4>
    source/code-first schema 需要稳定类型，body inference 会把运行时实现变成建模 authority。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS4>
    <evidence ?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS5>
    现有 accessor tests 与 mission single-authority rule。
    </?01KZKGVR657WGCDQ5KA09V2PS5>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.canonicalize_orm_annotations_with_named_conf.authority { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low" } (
  <question ?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQ9>
  How does NamedConf interact with Kunun's semantic authority and the retired ORM relation profile?
  </?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQ9>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQA>
    NamedConf is transport only; the public type-system model remains authority, and Kunun must not restore an ORM relation parser.
    </?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQA>
    <decision-text ?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQB>
    Existing datasource/entity/field profiles read NamedConf; typed Properties retain generic relation NamedConf for downstream consumers; no shadow model or public ORM relation descriptor is introduced.
    </?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQB>
    <rationale ?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQC>
    This keeps source-first and code-first on one model while preserving the property-first downstream ownership boundary.
    </?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQC>
    <evidence ?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQD>
    Parent mission design, archived behavior, current source, and fresh AttractorCheck.
    </?01KZNKRWXBXWZT1KJ34DGSNNQD>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.remove_orm_datasource_identity_duplication.public_surface { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true confidence = "high" reversibility = "low" } (
  <question ?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV90>
  Which surface owns datasource identity?
  </?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV90>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV91>
    Only the datasource declaration name.
    </?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV91>
    <decision-text ?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV92>
    ORM datasource annotation public types SHALL expose provider/environment/options only and SHALL NOT expose Key or Name.
    </?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV92>
    <rationale ?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV93>
    One stable declaration identity avoids dual source and public type authority.
    </?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV93>
    <evidence ?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV94>
    Parent mission P0 decision and fresh package verification.
    </?01KZNNMF632SHENVARZB2VZV94>
  )>
)>
